{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ec7e39d99b57bc5ac8", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Kinetic Theory of Gases - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c70"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c6d", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bed", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "What will be the effect on the root mean square velocity of oxygen molecules if the temperature is doubled and oxygen molecule dissociates into atomic oxygen?"}, "options": [{"id": "dae2fc", "text": "The velocity of atomic oxygen remains same", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bee"}, {"id": "f2852d", "text": "The velocity of atomic oxygen doubles", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bef"}, {"id": "2b26a0", "text": "The velocity of atomic oxygen becomes half", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf0"}, {"id": "31b87e", "text": "The velocity of atomic oxygen becomes four times", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c9"], "question": {"text": "A polyatomic ideal gas has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math> vibrational modes. What is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>?</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "bca209", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf3"}, {"id": "c3b066", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>30</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf4"}, {"id": "021ed2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>37</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf5"}, {"id": "4405d4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01f"], "question": {"text": "An ideal gas occupies a volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> at a pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The energy of the gas is:"}, "options": [{"id": "586382", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf8"}, {"id": "6d7f8e", "text": "<math><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bf9"}, {"id": "a85086", "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bfa"}, {"id": "b7cf88", "text": "<math><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bfb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bfc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566a"], "question": {"text": "To raise the temperature of a certain mass of gas by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> at a constant pressure,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>160</mn></math>&nbsp;calories of heat is required. When the same mass of gas is cooled by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> at constant volume,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>240</mn></math> calories of heat is released. How many degrees of freedom does each molecule of this gas have (assume gas to be ideal)?"}, "options": [{"id": "a36d37", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bfd"}, {"id": "9f8346", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bfe"}, {"id": "567ce0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233bff"}, {"id": "2cef81", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c00"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c01", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b5a"], "question": {"text": "Two vessels <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are of the same size and are at same temperature. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of hydrogen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of oxygen. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math> are the pressures of the gases in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> respectively, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "986bce", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c02"}, {"id": "0c6b88", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c03"}, {"id": "3948b1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c04"}, {"id": "d1bc66", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c05"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c06", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c682e"], "question": {"text": "The mean free path of molecules of a certain gas at STP is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1500</mn><mi>d</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>is the diameter of the gas molecules. While maintaining the standard pressure, the mean free path of the molecules at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>373</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>K</mi></math> is approximately:"}, "options": [{"id": "617924", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>750</mn><mi>d</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c07"}, {"id": "1a8d6b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1098</mn><mi>d</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c08"}, {"id": "18ff4b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2049</mn><mi>d</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c09"}, {"id": "0d3ec3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1500</mn><mi>d</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c0a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c0b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["61ab78d96fe44bfe0fe4a6ed"], "question": {"text": "The correct relation between the degrees of freedom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> and the ratio of specific heat <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "a8acf7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c0c"}, {"id": "f021f5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c0d"}, {"id": "cd14c3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c0e"}, {"id": "348a7b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c0f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c10", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["6162fb086ed13040ec84a448"], "question": {"text": "A gas mixture consists of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> moles of argon and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> moles of oxygen at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>. Neglecting all vibrational modes, the total internal energy of the system is"}, "options": [{"id": "9a30fd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>29</mn><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c11"}, {"id": "29c387", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c12"}, {"id": "90fc80", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c13"}, {"id": "ae5981", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c14"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c15", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["6162fb096ed13040ec84a530"], "question": {"text": "The relation between root mean square speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>rms</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub></mfenced></math> and most probable speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></mfenced></math> for the molar mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> of oxygen gas molecule at the temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> will be&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "1128df", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c16"}, {"id": "ec646b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c17"}, {"id": "c3680e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c18"}, {"id": "736bb1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c19"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c1a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52af"], "question": {"text": "When $100 \\mathrm{~g}$ of a liquid $\\mathrm{A}$ at $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is added to $50 \\mathrm{~g}$ of a liquid $B$ at temperature $75^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, the temperature of the mixture becomes $90^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The temperature of the mixture, if $100 \\mathrm{~g}$ of liquid $A$ at $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is added to $50 \\mathrm{~g}$ of liquid $\\mathrm{B}$ at $50^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "b2b1b0", "text": "$85^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c1b"}, {"id": "e50fdc", "text": "$60^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c1c"}, {"id": "406685", "text": "$80^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c1d"}, {"id": "acb0c9", "text": "$70^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c1e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c1f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "The ratio of vapour densities of two gases at the same temperature is $\\frac{4}{25}$, then the ratio of r.m.s. velocities will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "c8f07f", "text": "$\\frac{25}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c20"}, {"id": "2df22b", "text": "$\\frac{2}{5}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c21"}, {"id": "bcc60d", "text": "$\\frac{5}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c22"}, {"id": "b7d539", "text": "$\\frac{4}{25}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c23"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c24", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01f"], "question": {"text": "The average kinetic energy of a molecule of the gas is"}, "options": [{"id": "c53388", "text": "proportional to absolute temperature", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c25"}, {"id": "c4529c", "text": "proportional to volume", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c26"}, {"id": "e246e0", "text": "proportional to pressure", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c27"}, {"id": "ce3fe6", "text": "dependent on the nature of the gas", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c28"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c29", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f06"], "question": {"text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F6eaa6600-ba0e-42cc-9552-0d1c43adcbcb-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 148px;\" /></p><p>Consider a gas of triatomic molecules. The molecules&nbsp; are assumed to be triangular and made of massless rigid rods whose vertices are occupied by atoms. The internal energy of a mole of the gas at temperature T is:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b01bb9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c2a"}, {"id": "a81654", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c2b"}, {"id": "cf109f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c2c"}, {"id": "9d0a92", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c2d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c2e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b5a"], "question": {"text": "The volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> of an enclosure contains a mixture of three gases, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of oxygen,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>28</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of nitrogen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>44</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of carbon dioxide at absolute temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>. Consider <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> as universal gas constant. The pressure of the mixture of gases is :"}, "options": [{"id": "088040", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>88</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c2f"}, {"id": "07210f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c30"}, {"id": "5938c6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c31"}, {"id": "63a953", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c32"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c33", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "The root mean square speed of molecules of nitrogen gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is approximately: (Given mass of a nitrogen molecule <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>26</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and take Boltzmann constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>23</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )"}, "options": [{"id": "7b2d9a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c34"}, {"id": "6a613f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>91</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c35"}, {"id": "d6aaa1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1260</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c36"}, {"id": "5178b1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>523</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c37"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c38", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b54"], "question": {"text": "During an adiabatic process, if the pressure of a gas is found to be proportional to the cube of its absolute temperature, then the ratio of $\\frac{C_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{V}}}$ for the gas is :"}, "options": [{"id": "e96baf", "text": "$\\frac{5}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c39"}, {"id": "6f388c", "text": "$\\frac{9}{7}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c3a"}, {"id": "1fcbb9", "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c3b"}, {"id": "78c88b", "text": "$\\frac{7}{5}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c3c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c3d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["6162fb086ed13040ec84a448"], "question": {"text": "What will be the average value of energy for a monoatomic gas in thermal equilibrium at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>?</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "9097ef", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c3e"}, {"id": "59ade3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c3f"}, {"id": "b4ab19", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c40"}, {"id": "12eaae", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c41"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c42", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "The plot that depicts the behavior of the mean free time <math><mi>&#964;</mi></math> (time between two successive collisions) for the molecules of an ideal gas, as a function of temperature <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> qualitatively, is: (Graphs are schematic and not drawn to scale)"}, "options": [{"id": "a3fae9", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2a735d06-540d-4df9-836a-4af6c74c27a7-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 149px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c43"}, {"id": "63bb00", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F72317618-59b5-49b8-b6b2-dae2aca77a62-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 175px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c44"}, {"id": "7d85da", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fca63f38e-fc46-43af-a1a3-63ef0e8658ed-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 175px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c45"}, {"id": "4603bb", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8e5f41c9-ecbb-4060-86bb-ea8d6e183d0f-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 149px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c46"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c47", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2e"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> mass of nitrogen gas is enclosed in a vessel at a temperature,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>27</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.&nbsp;The amount of heat transferred to the gas, so that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>.</mo></math> velocity of molecules is doubled, is about.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.3</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mole</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "7ac57f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c48"}, {"id": "c85fee", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c49"}, {"id": "2d7026", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c4a"}, {"id": "af5b7a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.9</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c4b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c4c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01f"], "question": {"text": "The helium and argon are put in the flask at the same room temperature ( 300 K). The ratio of average kinetic energies (per molecule) of helium and argon is :<br/>(Give : Molar mass of helium $=4 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}$, Molar mass of argon $=40 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}$)"}, "options": [{"id": "22d7bb", "text": "$1: 10$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c4d"}, {"id": "0bf395", "text": "$10: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c4e"}, {"id": "f416fc", "text": "$1: \\sqrt{10}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c4f"}, {"id": "6a6e2c", "text": "$1: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c50"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c51", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p><strong>Statement I :</strong>The average momentum of a molecule in a sample of an ideal gas depends on temperature.</p><p><strong>Statement II :</strong> The rms speed of oxygen molecules in a gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. If the temperature is doubled and the oxygen molecules dissociate into oxygen atoms, the rms speed will become <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "0b05d2", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c52"}, {"id": "519b75", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c53"}, {"id": "9d2461", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c54"}, {"id": "678c35", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c55"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c56", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c9"], "question": {"text": "<p>According to kinetic theory of gases,</p><p>A. The motion of the gas molecules freezes at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</p><p>B. The mean free path of gas molecules decreases if the density of molecules is increased.</p><p>C. The mean free path of gas molecules increases if temperature is increased keeping pressure constant.</p><p>D. Average kinetic energy per molecule per degree of freedom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math> (for monoatomic gases).</p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a827ec", "text": "A and C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c57"}, {"id": "bbdf5a", "text": "B and C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c58"}, {"id": "4b8227", "text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c59"}, {"id": "cc6a66", "text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c5a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c5b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["6162fb086ed13040ec84a448"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement I: In a diatomic molecule, the rotational energy at a given temperature obeys Maxwell&#39;s distribution.</p><p>Statement II : In a diatomic molecule, the rotational energy at a given temperature equals the translational kinetic energy for each molecule.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ac106e", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;is false but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c5c"}, {"id": "7a2587", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is true but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c5d"}, {"id": "5f1d14", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c5e"}, {"id": "06a102", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c5f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c60", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "Assuming the nitrogen molecule is moving with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. velocity at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the de-Broglie wave length of nitrogen molecule is close to : (Given : nitrogen molecule weight :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.64</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>26</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>kg</mi></math>, Boltzman constant :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.38</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>23</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, Planck constant :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.63</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "262277", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c61"}, {"id": "e4116b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c62"}, {"id": "39ebea", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>34</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c63"}, {"id": "a2d178", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>44</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c64"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c65", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566a"], "question": {"text": "A metal ball of mass $0.1 \\mathrm{~kg}$ is heated upto $500^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and dropped into a vessel of heat capacity $800 \\mathrm{JK}^{-1}$ and containing $0.5 \\mathrm{~kg}$ water. The initial temperature of water and vessel is $30^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. What is the approximate percentage increment in the temperature of the water? [Specific Heat Capacities of water and metal are, respectively, $4200 \\mathrm{Jkg}^{-}$ ${ }^{1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}$ and $400 \\mathrm{Jkg}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}$ ]"}, "options": [{"id": "a6991a", "text": "$15 \\%$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c66"}, {"id": "443901", "text": "$30 \\%$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c67"}, {"id": "c050c6", "text": "$25 \\%$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c68"}, {"id": "da26ad", "text": "$20 \\%$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f132ee0e063d9233c69"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximu